sis-map-uib-ws","line":86},{"title":"Configure a form header for a workspace","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/config-ws-form-header.md","line":105},{"title":"crisis events","target":"crisis-management-uib","line":111},{"title":"Configure alert actions","target":"configure-alert-action-uib-ws","line":123},{"title":"Structured workflows for Crisis map","target":"crisis-map-collective-tasks","line":129},{"title":"Configure Resource Configuration records","target":"conf-resource-for-crisis-map-uib-ws","line":133},{"title":"Configure alert actions","target":"configure-alert-action-uib-ws","line":134},{"title":"Structured workflows for Crisis map","target":"crisis-map-collective-tasks","line":135},{"title":"Crisis events","target":"crisis-management-uib","line":136}],"metadata":{"title":"Enhanced Performance with UIB pages","description":"The Crisis map application is now built with a UI Builder \\(UIB\\) page. Previously, the single-use component limited the ability to customize the user interface \\(UI\\), add filters, or modify the design in the Crisis map. By adopting the UIB page, you can gain full control over the implementation, enabling you to extend support for your specific use cases.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/governance-risk-compliance/crisis-map-migration.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":7,"breadcrumb":["Structured workflows for Crisis map","Manage","Business Continuity Management","Governance","Risk","and Compliance"],"tags":["#governance-risk-compliance","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/governance-risk-compliance/crisis-map-migration.md"},
